light:

  rect 2 15 7 3 3       ; entry hall
  rect 9 12 8 9 4       ; junction -- lit enough to read the red door
  cell 17 15 7
  cell 17 16 6
  cell 17 17 7          ; torches flanking the locked door: look HERE
  rect 12 9 2 3 1       ; north corridor, dark
  rect 5 2 16 7 5       ; the cistern is open and bright
  rect 6 5 14 1 6       ; the nukage channel glows
  rect 2 5 2 3 4        ; secret vault
  rect 14 21 2 3 1      ; south corridor, dark
  rect 7 24 12 5 3      ; armoury, dim
  rect 18 16 4 1 2      ; behind the red door: dark again
  rect 22 9 7 16 5      ; finale hall
  rect 24 24 2 1 7      ; the exit switch
end

notes:

THE RED CISTERN -- show the locked door on the way IN, not on the way back.

  1 SPAWN (3,16) facing east down a 3-wide entry hall. Columns at (5,15) and
    (6,17) sit OFF the centre line -- row 16 is kept clear from the spawn all
    the way to the door -- so the first frame has near silhouettes on both
    flanks and a clear axis between them. At this range the far end is only a
    suggestion; the corridor is the dark, tight half of the rhythm.
  2 JUNCTION (x9-16 y12-20, light 4). Four or five steps in, at about six
    cells, the far wall resolves and it is unmistakable: two glowing cells at
    (16,15) and (16,17) stand one cell PROUD of the wall and between them is
    a recessed slab. Because the frame is geometry and not just colour, the
    door reads as a door on a renderer that does not yet draw materials. It
    IS a door, it IS locked, and it is the only lit thing you have seen.
    Landmark #1: every route from here is "back to the red door".
  3 Two exits, north (x12-13) and south (x14-15), both dark one-cell
    corridors. The level forks and neither fork is the door.
  4 NORTH -> THE CISTERN (x5-20 y2-8, light 5). Sixteen cells across, split by
    a glowing nukage channel at y5 that hurts to cross, with two rows of
    broken rock columns so both banks read as space rather than void. The
    channel is breached only at its ends (x5, x20): you can SEE the far bank
    the whole time and you can see the price of the short route.
  5 The RED KEY at (18,3) sits on the far bank with a gunner either side and a
    rock column at (19,3) for them to fight from. Reward visible, cost visible.
  6 SECRET: the cistern's west wall at (4,6) is fake. Armour + shells.
  7 SOUTH -> THE ARMOURY (x7-18 y24-28, light 3). Optional, and signposted as
    optional by being dim and dead-ended. Holds the AUTOGUN. Exploring makes
    you measurably stronger for the finale; skipping it blocks nothing.
  8 BACK TO THE DOOR along a route you already know -- the payoff for having
    made the door a landmark in beat 2.
  9 FINALE HALL (x22-28 y9-24, light 5). Tall, not wide: seven cells across
    and sixteen deep, columned on a 3-cell pitch, so from the entrance at its
    waist you look down two long aisles in opposite directions and cannot see
    both ends at once. A hulk at (26,16) is on you immediately; spitters hold
    the far ends. Exit at the bottom (x24-25 y24).
end
